  "headline": "FDA's records show the product labeler Preferred Pharmaceuticals Inc. received a VAI classification on 2025-05-27",
  "headline_cites": ["E9", "E8"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "The sertraline hydrochloride 25 mg tablets used across Corvale sites carry NDC 68788404503 and are labeled by Preferred Pharmaceuticals Inc. per SPL set 8f5a71b2.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E2", "E3", "E9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1270956 of the labeler's facility (FEI 3004582966) ended on 2025-05-27 and was classified VAI, with the classification known on 2025-07-30.",
      "cites": ["E8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Earlier inspections of the same facility in 2009, 2015, 2018, and 2020 were also classified VAI.",
      "cites": ["E4", "E5", "E6", "E7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale Lakeside holds 15 units at 1.8 per day, giving 9 days on hand, while Corvale East holds 208 units at 6.7 per day, giving 31 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D3", "D1"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale General holds 225 units at 7.9 per day, giving 29 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the links between the shortage and the inspection record are weak, verify current allocation policies and confirm whether the labeler has communicated any supply constraints.",
      "cites": ["E8", "E9"]
    }
  ]
}
